 "captions": {
  "script": "Where on Earth do hundreds of balloons rise over stone towers every sunrise? This is Cappadocia, in central Turkey. These fairy chimneys were carved by wind and rain from volcanic ash that settled here millions of years ago. People dug homes, churches and even whole cities into the soft rock. The underground city of Derinkuyu goes about eighty-five metres deep. And since nineteen eighty-five, it has been a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Would you fly here at sunrise? Which country should we show next?",
